          "note": "Roman Urdu explanation of accessing list items (PDF 51)."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "List ke items un ke index (number) se nikale jate hain, aur index 0 se shuru hota hai. Misaal: fruits list ka doosra item print karein."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "language": "python",
            "text": "fruits = [\"Mango\", \"Apple\", \"Banana\"]\nprint(fruits [1])\n# Output: Apple"
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Kitab ki ghalti",
            "text": "Kitab list ko tirchhi (curly) quotes, ek faltu quote aur bina band bracket ke chhapti hai (”Apple”, “” Banana”); aise SyntaxError aata hai. Sahi: fruits = [\"Mango\", \"Apple\", \"Banana\"]."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Wazahat: list mein 'Mango' index 0, 'Apple' index 1 aur 'Banana' index 2 par hain. fruits[1] doosra item 'Apple' deta hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "fruits[0] aur fruits[2] kya hain?",
            "explanation": "fruits[0] 'Mango' aur fruits[2] 'Banana' hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Mukhtasar khulasa"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Index 0 se shuru: pehla item fruits[0], doosra fruits[1]."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
